# Auth and session

Better Auth owns the cookie. TanStack Query owns the `{ session, user } | null` view of it. TanStack Router owns whether the user is allowed on the URL.

## Pieces (do not duplicate)

| File | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `packages/auth` | Server `betterAuth(...)` |
| `routes/api/auth/$.ts` | Forwards GET/POST to `auth.handler` |
| `lib/auth/auth-client.ts` | `createAuthClient({})` — same-origin `/api/auth` |
| `middleware/auth.ts` | `sessionMiddleware` → `auth.api.getSession({ headers })` |
| `functions/get-session.ts` | Server fn returning `{ session, user } \| null` |
| `lib/auth/session.ts` | `SESSION_QUERY_KEY` + `sessionQueryOptions` |
| `lib/auth/auth-redirect.ts` | Open-redirect safe path + real-route check |
| `hooks/use-user.ts` | `useSuspenseQuery` — only inside `/dashboard` |

Do not call `authClient.useSession()` for route gates. Do not add a second session cache.

## Redirects (`beforeLoad` only)

| Route | Has session | No session |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/` | → `/dashboard` | → `/sign-in` |
| `/_auth` | → `safeRedirectPath(search.redirect) ?? "/dashboard"` | stay |
| `/dashboard` | stay | → `/sign-in?redirect=<location.href>` |

After `authClient.signIn.email` succeeds: `invalidateQueries({ queryKey: SESSION_QUERY_KEY })`, then `router.navigate({ href: resolvePostAuthRedirect(router, redirectParam), replace: true })`.

After `signOut`: `removeQueries({ queryKey: SESSION_QUERY_KEY })`, navigate to `/sign-in` with `replace: true`, then `cancelQueries` + `clear()`.

`?redirect=` must pass `safeRedirectPath` (starts with `/`, not `//`). Post-login also requires `router.getMatchedRoutes` to hit a real route; otherwise `/dashboard`.

## Mutations

Sign-in / sign-up / sign-out go through `authClient`, not tRPC. Domain APIs use `protectedProcedure` and read `ctx.session` — they do not re-implement login.
